  "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the nets of each solid.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248692/assets/e9168bf41b10db4e0d353aa09682a7fe048216a0ccf28fd196daaf5bf7fd3fff.png)\n\n \n\nAs we can see, the correct answer is:\n\n$\\,$ *\"The net of III consists of $1$ rectangle and $4$ triangles.\"*\n\nOther statements are false. \n\n- *\"The net of II consists of triangles only\"* is false since the net of II has $3$ rectangles (the side faces).\n\n- *\"The net of I has one triangle\"* is not true because the net of I contains only squares.\n\n- *\"The net of III consists of $4$ triangles and $2$ rectangles\"* is false since the net of III only has $1$ rectangle (the base of the solid).\n\n- *\"The net of I consists of exactly $8$ squares\"* is not true because the net of I only has $6$ squares.",
